<p><strong><em>Far From the Madding Crowd, </em>Thomas Hardy</strong></p>
<p>“‘Why, Gabriel,’ she said, with a slight laugh, as they went to the door, ‘it seems exactly as if I had come courting you—how dreadful!’</p>
<p>“‘And quite right, too,’ said Oak. ‘I’ve danced at your skittish heels, my beautiful Bathsheba, for many a long mile, and many a long day and it is hard to begrudge me this one visit.’”</p>
